# campaign.rules — yamlmuster ruleset for a campaign YAML
# (campaigns/<campaign>.yaml): the closed vocabulary of every level
# spar-campaign-yaml.md documents, so a key an author or agent invents is
# reported instead of sitting unread. Loaded by spar::_yamlmuster_campaign and
# driven by spar::validate_campaign_yaml.
#
# Call shape:
#   validate <view> -groups {campaign} -badnode ignore
# where <view> is the loaded campaign dict as validate_campaign_yaml reshapes
# it: the loader's own `_`-prefixed keys dropped, and the two name-keyed maps
# (segments, usps) handed over as lists of their values, since a child edge
# walks one dict or a list of dicts. -badnode ignore skips the scalar forms
# the document allows beside a block: a bare primary_channel name, a
# list-form segments entry, a label-only USP.
#
# The loader lifts a 2.0 file's usp_document into fact_sources and drops it
# before this runs, so it is not vocabulary here. Required keys are not
# checked here: missing version is validate_versions', and the sender block
# is validate_sender_block's (send readiness, not data integrity).

# ── Levels ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each -keys list mirrors a table in spar-campaign-yaml.md; change both
# together.
level root              -keys {version campaign start_date sender language \
                               segments usps primary_channel secondary_channel \
                               tertiary_channel filter fact_sources antifacts \
                               campaign_principles ses_region a_max_passes \
                               worker_cost_cap_usd reply_check prompt_appendices}
level sender            -keys {name role email organisation bcc \
                               smtp_host smtp_port smtp_user smtp_pass}
level channel           -keys {channel wait_days wait_condition}
level filter            -keys {skip_excluded min_star require_profile}
level reply_check       -keys {mailbox folder}
level prompt_appendices -keys {p_author a_author a_challenger a_assembly}
level usp_entry         -keys {label rests_on claim}
level plan              -keys {objective usps message_goal first_ask ask_stance \
                               recipient_problem deciding_interest state_want \
                               conversion_funnel approach_sequencing subsegments \
                               stems}
level plan_usp          -keys {id type framing}
level funnel_step       -keys {step name description}
level sequencing_step   -keys {step action}

child root sender            dict sender
child root primary_channel   dict channel
child root secondary_channel dict channel
child root tertiary_channel  dict channel
child root filter            dict filter
child root reply_check       dict reply_check
child root prompt_appendices dict prompt_appendices
child root usps              list usp_entry
child root segments          list plan
child plan usps                list plan_usp
child plan conversion_funnel   list funnel_step
child plan approach_sequencing list sequencing_step
# subsegments stays un-levelled: the spec names the fields a subsegment may
# override but not the key that names one.

# ── Rules ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
rule vocab root              -groups {campaign}
rule vocab sender            -groups {campaign}
rule vocab channel           -groups {campaign}
rule vocab filter            -groups {campaign}
rule vocab reply_check       -groups {campaign}
rule vocab prompt_appendices -groups {campaign}
rule vocab usp_entry         -groups {campaign}
rule vocab plan              -groups {campaign}
rule vocab plan_usp          -groups {campaign}
rule vocab funnel_step       -groups {campaign}
rule vocab sequencing_step   -groups {campaign}
